            "review_title": "Review at M.Oi Bistro & Bar",
            "review_text": "Bahr W\nDa Nang, Vietnam9 contributions\n0\nGreat new resaurant in Danang, with great Vietnamese and Western cuisine\nJan 2024 • Couples\nSome friends recommended this place. It just opened a couple of weeks ago, and right now (Jan 2024) it's only open for breakfast, it will be fully open after they have finished the remodeling, in late Feb after Tet. But we wanted to give it a try.\n\nSo, what was it like? The food is great! My wife, who is Vietnamese, and I had a traditional Western breakfast, I had fried eggs, bacon, potatoes, tomato, etc. She had eggs benedict. But the menu is a nice balance of Western food (like we had) and Vietnamese food. My breakfast was great, the eggs were cooked perfect, the bacon was some of the best bacon I've ever had, not too much fat, and very tasty. The bread was nice, to soak up the egg yolk. I tried my wife's eggs benedict (of course) and it was great too, nice creamy rich flavor. The drinks were great too, I had carrot and orange juice combo, which turned out to be a great combination, the flavors balance each other really well. I (of course) tried my wife's green matcha tea, and I ended up getting one for myself. The staff are pleasant and helpful but not hovering.\n\nThe restaurant itself is quite nice, pleasant, there's an outdoor area with a little fish pond and some trees, very pleasant, and the indoor area is clean and comfortable.\n\nWe will definitely being going back when it opens for lunch and dinner in a month. And probably for breakfast again before that!\nRead more\nWritten January 26, 2024",
